WEBVTT

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.370
When his thoughts are of life,

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.930
and he accepts everything, his eyes open.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.860
Hirose...

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.410
And his eyes close into darkness

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.790
when death takes over his mind,

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.900
and he denies the entire world.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.790
What he chose was...

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.140
I'm going to protect my mother!

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.700
Hirose...

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.430
Don't hurt my mother!

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.340
Get lost!

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.740
Get lost!

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.850
Go!

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.170
What are you doing, Takuma-kun?

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.360
Shut up!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.380
Stay away! Stay away!

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.380
Hirose!

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.360
Stay away!

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.430
No more!

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.660
Release me!

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.830
Let me go!

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.050
Please!

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.490
Mom...

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.000
Hirose?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.040
Hirose!

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.030
Hayami-chan! Hayami-chan!

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.800
Over here, Hotaru!

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.910
Tacky!

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.850
I called the police.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.310
What?

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.480
I'm going to tell them everything.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.730
That the guns were missing from our home...

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.460
That you were here...

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.720
You little...

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.530
The village is not your property!

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.840
Tacky!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.310
It's me! Do you recognize me?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.650
Tacky...

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.190
Where's my mom?

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.920
Where's my mom?

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:34.540
<b>Twelfth Hour: H2O</b>

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.870
He can't control the memories

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.300
that he subconsciously repressed.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.900
Then what's he going to...

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.280
If you try to force him to accept reality,

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.370
he's going to reject it.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:52.310
For a while, you need to accept how he is.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.150
Accept it...

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.040
Mom!

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.380
You're here. Aren't you, Mom?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.490
Mom.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.820
I'm here.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.380
Hold my hand.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.030
Don't let go, okay?

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.810
<b>Sawaii Village Head Arrested
for Attempted Murder</b>

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:20.940
She's here!

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.580
Can we talk to you for a minute?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.310
Did you hate your grandfather?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:30.550
Um...

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.930
There are some people in the village

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.220
who criticize what you did,

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.150
saying that it was some kind of power struggle.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.090
<i>Shelling Kick!</i>

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.690
Get lost, cockroach!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.890
What?

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:48.000
Oh, no! He touched me in my special place!

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.370
I-I-I-Impossible...

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.310
It's so heavy!

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.490
What are you doing?

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:56.510
S-Stop it!

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.910
They really are persistent.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.360
It can't be helped.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.550
What I did was that momentous...

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.870
What?

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.660
You did the right thing.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:12.480
Right!

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.250
Yukiji was saying if those guys came back,
they'd take care of them.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.810
Everyone's on your side.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.030
Anyway, it's about time for Hirose to return.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.380
Your arm's better, right?

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.390
Yes.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.250
At the hospital, I had them look at it,
and they said it was fine.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.250
What about Hirose?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:40.950
He's okay, right?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.990
To Tokyo?

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:52.710
They said it'd be better if he were closer

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.700
to places he'd been with his mother.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:56.530
You can't mean...

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:59.400
Hirose and I are going to Tokyo.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.750
I don't have a house,
so it doesn't matter where I go.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.010
No way...

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.170
But Hirose-kun is...

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.110
Maki!

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.520
It's strange...

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.740
All this is happening, but for
some reason, I'm happy.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.800
When I think that someone needs me...

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.700
Starting tomorrow, you have to do it yourself.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:26.930
Okay!

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.870
Goodnight, then!

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.310
Goodnight.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.770
Anything you forgot?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.680
No.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.970
I don't have many things anyway.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.300
This is your apartment's address.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.160
Ever since Tacky's mom died,

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.840
the Hirose family's rented it under their name.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.020
It's just as it was.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.490
What about the rest of his family?

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:57.860
They say they want nothing to do with it.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.680
They just ask that his symptoms
are kept quiet.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.570
That's all.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.540
I see.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:08.100
No sense in looking for anything from them.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.870
You'll have to reveal the way yourself.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.640
Yes, I understand.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.970
No need to tell you, huh?

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.150
I'm going out for a while.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.520
Yeah. It's your last time, isn't it?

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.380
<i>Wait!</i>

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:55.640
<i>Hamaji!</i>

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.660
They're all painful memories,

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.410
but now that I'm leaving, it's kind of sad.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.600
It's been a long time.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.510
Yes.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.370
We've come this whole way together.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:57.830
We've hurt each other so much, we've clashed,

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:01.150
tripped, burned...

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.430
Gotten frostbite...

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.990
Thought we didn't want
to go on, still hurting...

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:11.960
And then, finally, we learned to
take each other's hand.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.970
At last, we learned to support one another.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:20.290
Now I can say it with pride...

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.340
Kagura Hotaru is my dear friend.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:27.950
Yes... So even if we're apart, we're okay.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:30.650
Really?

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.270
Hayami-chan...

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.690
I... I...

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:42.860
I won't forget you.

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.400
Right!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:56.800
Hirose Takuma-kun has transferred to a
small reception care for his illness.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.040
It was a short time,

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:02.040
but he was happy to make friends with you all.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:04.370
That's what he said.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:09.850
And Hayami Kohinata is transferring, too.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:13.020
She won't be coming back, she says.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:16.260
You really don't need to say goodbyes?

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.100
School's almost over.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.420
Yes.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:21.030
I've already done it.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.480
I see.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:24.840
K-Kohinata...

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.930
You guys...

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.560
We're sorry!

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:31.440
We're sorry!

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:35.610
Mom! Are you ready?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.700
Yes, I'll be right there.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.120
Um...

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.020
Take care of Hotaru.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:46.310
Kohinata...

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:55.030
Remember me, now and again, okay?

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:59.000
Hey, Mom...

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.340
Can we hold hands?

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:03.880
Yes.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:04.980
We can.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.000
Um...

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.900
This way!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:32.340
Jeez, did you forget your own house, Mom?

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:36.270
We're back.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:48.150
This is the room where you
lived with your mom.

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.550
Everyone,

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:02.600
the calendar says it's fall,
but the hot days continue.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:07.640
I'm sure you're all doing well, as usual.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.010
We're as fine as ever.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.510
I'm finally used to my job.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.970
But the city streets are complex, as always.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:18.450
Why do they make diagonal streets?

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:22.350
I'd expect people to just get lost...

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:25.650
Hirose hasn't changed much.

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.450
But sometimes,

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.990
he has his old expressions and mannerisms.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:37.560
I know he doesn't mean to,
but sometimes, he causes trouble.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.810
Oh, there is one change!

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.140
Hayami?

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.140
Yeah... She was in a dream.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.990
Do you know her?

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:53.150
What kind of girl was she?

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:56.780
She always had these scary eyes.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:58.410
And she was quiet...

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.760
Even when I talked to her, she ignored me.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.630
And she always hit me.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:05.330
But...

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.820
She was nice.

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.530
And she gave me ramen!

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.500
Mom?

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.110
Hey... Do you like her?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:23.980
You do!

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:27.790
I... I don't know!

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.210
I was happy.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:33.320
I thought, I'm still inside him.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:35.880
I thought, I haven't disappeared.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.820
That's how things are for now.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.000
If anything else happens, I'll let you know.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.160
Soon, it will get colder.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:47.810
Please take care.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:49.280
P.S.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:52.080
I heard that Tabata-san
changed her hairstyle.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:54.160
I'd like to see it.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.650
I'm back.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.640
Welcome back!

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:03.880
Wait a bit.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.340
I'm going to go buy food.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:08.290
Then I'll go, too.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:10.080
Don't be selfish.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.500
I'll be back soon.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:16.370
I'm sick of staying here alone!

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.230
Oh, fine.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:22.440
Get ready.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:23.870
Okay!

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:47.760
Hey...

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.100
Takuma.

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:51.240
What is it, Mom?

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.970
What do you think of your mom?

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:58.120
Why?

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:01.010
Why do you think she left you behind?

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.940
You're always with me.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:06.580
Your real mom...

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:13.460
I can't believe she left you behind.

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:18.400
She wouldn't do that.

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:31.010
Listen!

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:35.350
Your mother loved you.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:38.150
I think your mother loved you
more than anything.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:48.530
So believe in your mother's feelings.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:52.520
My mother's feelings...

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.290
No...

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:33.900
No!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.510
<i>That's right!</i>

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.060
<i>Back then...</i>

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.470
<i>My mom...</i>

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.090
<i>Accept it all, okay?</i>

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:59.030
Hayami-chan!

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:02.530
Hayami-chan!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.890
Hirose Takuma-sama,

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:31.260
I'll never have a chance to
tell you these feelings.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:35.130
You and I are too far away,

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:40.620
and I am far from capable of putting
these feelings into words.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:44.880
So I'm thinking, I'll write you now, here.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:52.980
You taught me that there is light in the sky,

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:55.890
and that water washes things away.

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.060
And the wind brings change.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:02.350
The words can be a sharp blade

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.520
and an enveloping kindness,
at the same time...

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:07.430
That even if we can't understand one another,

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:09.390
humans have hearts,

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:11.640
and so someone is sure to notice.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:14.570
When I knew nothing...

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.740
And had given up on everything...

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.710
And had thrown it all away...

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.450
You taught me these things, one by one.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:26.890
As best you could, without giving in,

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.350
tightly clasping my hand.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.390
The word "like" is too easy.

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:37.890
The word "love" is too vague.

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:41.130
So I don't know what's best to write,

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:44.200
what embodies these words.

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:50.670
<b>Hirose,
Thank you for the world.</b>

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:48.580
I don't know, so this is what I will write...

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.280
<i>You were with me</i>

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.780
<i>all those times I was happy,</i>

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.920
<i>all the good times in my life.</i>

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.700
<i>But why, when I</i>

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:09.000
<i>needed you most by my side,</i>

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:13.200
<i>have you not been there for me?</i>

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.820
God replied to the man,

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:20.000
<i>I would never leave you.</i>

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.570
<i>But when you were suffering from anguish</i>

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:25.820
<i>or drowning in your sorrows,</i>

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:28.550
<i>it was then that I carried you.</i>

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:30.160
And the man looked at God.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:33.540
And for everything God had done, he said...

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:35.730
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.870
That's impossible.

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:59.810
You refuse the request of the great Yui-sama?

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:03.560
Even if you're asking, we can't do what we can't do.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:05.720
The village's fields belong to everyone.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:08.190
I just want to borrow them for a little bit!

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.850
If one person cheats like that,

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.070
it changes the whole village for the worse!

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:15.760
As the Village Head, I refuse to allow it.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:20.900
Stop looking down on me like that!

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.660
But I'm standing above you...

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.770
Hello!

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:24.940
Maki-san!

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:27.140
I was nearby, so I thought I'd say hi.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:31.180
Are you still slacking off here, Yui-chan?

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:35.500
Oh, my... He looks more
like his father every day.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.980
Why do you look so unhappy?

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:48.560
You're wearing that again?

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.760
You need to give it up, already.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.080
It's fine.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.600
Anyway, how are things going with it?

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.600
They said it's done today.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:02.790
I see.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:19.490
We're ready, Tacky!

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:21.860
Stop calling me Tacky.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:24.730
I'm not a kid anymore.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:32.050
We made it pretty tough.

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:35.090
It'd take quite a storm to knock it down.

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:35.990
Yeah.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:39.340
Think she'd be happy?

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:40.510
I think so.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:44.050
Hayami-chan loved windmills.

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.580
I see.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.250
Hayami-chan.

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:02.770
Save me!

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:07.200
Angry charging boar!

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.390
You're...

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:29.120
Otoha!

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:30.390
Where are you?

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:31.560
Over here!

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:33.840
I'll be right there!

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:35.500
Otoha?

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:41.560
It's been a while.

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:42.910
You've grown up.

00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:45.700
It was really hard, getting this request

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:47.280
granted at the Spirit Council.

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:52.310
So this time, protect her, okay?

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:56.520
Wait!

00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:58.540
What was that?

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:29.280
A beautiful wind...

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:36.960
Hayami-chan...

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:11.350
Hirose...
